  "description": "Commands every agent client must ask the user to confirm, and files it must not read. Gate only irreversible or outward-facing actions; routine work the policy already authorizes (commits on a work branch, issue comments, status updates) is not gated. A safety backstop for the work policy authority rules: answering a prompt never grants commit, publication or merge authority, and prefix rules can be bypassed (gh api, git -C, shell wrappers). retired lists shared commands that sync removes from consumer lists and Claude settings. Run npm run handbook:sync after editing to update .claude/settings.json; handbook:entrypoints reports missing or retired entries. Projects may add entries; shared entries are merged add-only except retired ones.",
